  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <p>Looking for a beach where dogs are accepted in Six-Fours-les-Plages? Brutal Beach sets aside a dedicated area on Bonnegrâce beach.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Bonnegrâce is the largest beach in Six-Fours: about 1.2 km of fine gravel along the Promenade Charles-de-Gaulle, with restaurants, beach establishments, paid parking and a Blue Flag (Provence Méditerranée tourist office). At its far end, towards La Coudoulière, a portion goes by the everyday name "Brutal Beach": it is the meeting point of surfers and windsurfers when the mistral raises good waves. It is on this portion that the town hall has marked out a dog area, which it officially calls "Plage Amie des Animaux". It extends over 50 metres, at the southern end of the beach, on the Rayon de Soleil esplanade side (town publication of 12 June).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The rules posted by the town are as follows: dogs on a leash, respect for other users and for calm, waste systematically picked up, constant supervision of the animal, respect for swimming hours and zones. Dogs are allowed except 1st- and 2nd-category dogs, and you must stay within the 50-metre limits. Board sports are practised in the same sector: keep your dog close.</p>
      <p>The ground is gravel, not fine sand: think of your dog's paw pads in the hot hours. The beach is supervised from May to the end of September. Showers are accessible from 9am to 7pm while the lifeguard posts are open, but soap is not allowed, which makes a proper rinse of the dog difficult. Parking is paid along the promenade; the tourist office mentions a bus stop less than 500 m away.</p>
      <p>For any question about the rule in force, the Six-Fours municipal police can be reached on 04 94 34 94 20 (Monday to Friday, 8am-12pm and 1:30pm-4:30pm).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: head to the Presqu'île du Gaou and its shaded trails at the end of the day to extend the outing without the heat.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed on Bonnegrâce beach?</h3>
      <p>Yes, in a dedicated 50-metre area, officially named "Plage Amie des Animaux" by the town hall.</p>
      <h3>Is a leash compulsory?</h3>
      <p>Yes, leash compulsory; access is free (tourist office).</p>
      <h3>Which dogs are excluded from this area?</h3>
      <p>Category 1 and 2 dogs.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Île du Grand Gaou and its trails, a few minutes south of Six-Fours, make a possible continuation of the walk after the beach; check the dog rule with the commune before going.</p>
